Section: devel
Priority: required
Standards-Version: 4.5.1

Package: hdctools-docker-fake
Version: 9999-1
Maintainer: The ChromiumOS Authors <chromium-os-dev@chromium.org>
Provides: libflashrom1 (= 1.3.9999-1), libflashrom-dev, libusb-1.0-0 (= 2:1.0.9999-1), libusb-1.0-0-dev, libftdi1-2 (= 1.5.9999-1), libftdi1-dev
Conflicts: libflashrom1, libflashrom-dev, libusb-1.0-0, libusb-1.0-0-dev, libftdi1-2, libftdi1-dev
Architecture: all
Description: Stand-In for locally installed sources
 The hdctools Docker container builds a couple of libraries and tools on
 its own for various reasons: With some, we need a custom version (e.g.
 flashrom), others need different compilation flags to work properly in
 the container context (e.g. libusb). To avoid mixing up two versions in
 the container, we fake the presence of the distro packages for the things
 we install on our own. This is an easier approach than maintaining those
 packages as Debian packages ourselves.
